<div class="faq-section">
  <!-- Student Q&A --> <h2>Student Q&A: Emerging Fields After PUC</h2>
  
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>Do I need a degree to work in AI/Data Science/Cyber Security?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
No. Many professionals in these fields are self-taught or bootcamp grads. What matters is demonstrable skills: GitHub repos, project write-ups, certifications, and problem-solving ability. A degree can help with structure and networking - but it's not mandatory.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>How do I choose between AI, Cyber Security, Cloud, or UX?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Don't chase 'trending' names. Ask: 'What will I do daily?' If you love coding + math, pick AI/Data. If you love systems + problem-solving, pick Cyber Security/Cloud. If you love users + design, pick UX/Product. If unsure, start with foundational Python + SQL - it applies to all.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>What if I'm from a tier-2/3 city in Karnataka?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
You don't need to relocate to Bangalore. Remote work is common in emerging fields. Focus on building a strong online portfolio, participating in virtual communities (C2 Club, Discord, LinkedIn), and applying for remote internships. Location is less important than connectivity and output.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>How do I get my first internship or freelance gig?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Start by Month 3-6 of learning: build 1-2 small projects, document them publicly, and share on LinkedIn/C2 Club. Apply to internships via AngelList, Wellfound, or C2 Club referrals. For freelance, start with small local businesses or Upwork gigs to build testimonials.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>Can I switch from engineering/medical to emerging fields later?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Yes. Many professionals pivot from traditional degrees to emerging fields. Your domain knowledge (e.g., healthcare + AI, agriculture + data) can be a unique advantage. Start with foundational courses, build projects that combine your background + new skills, and network via C2 Club.
</p> </div> </details>
</div>









